 "name": "Blazing Courage (Major Innate Technique)",
 "type": "feat",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/feat.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Creeps and Curses V.3.1</em></p><p><em>Major Innate Technique. Example technique for sorcerers and NPCs (GM approval).</em></p><p><strong>Ignition</strong></p>\n<p>You can spend up to your CE modifier (min of 1) as a bonus action while holding a melee weapon, igniting said weapon in flames for 1 minute. For the duration, the weapon deals 1d8 fire damage on a hit per CE spent. When using Ignition you ignore any detriments or penalties of the weapon or can use it on yourself for your unarmed strikes, potentially recreating a lost limb for the duration.</p>\n<p><strong>Mantle of Courage</strong></p>\n<p>While Ignition is active, you can spend 3 CE as a free action. You emit an aura of flames within 10 feet of you for 1 minute, giving you resistance to fire and cold damage. A creature that enters your mantle or starts their turn there must make a Constitution saving throw, taking your Ignition damage on a failed save or half as much on a successful save.</p>\n<p><strong>Burning Rend</strong></p>\n<p>While Ignition is active, you can spend 1 cursed energy to launch a burning slash, increasing the range of one of your melee attacks to 30 ft. This later increases to 60 ft.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
